window.EXTRA={
solar:[["Moons","Earth’s Moon formed about 4.5 billion years ago, most likely from debris after a Mars-sized body struck the young Earth. Saturn has more than 200 known moons."]],
photo:[["Beyond plants","Ocean algae produce a large share of Earth’s oxygen. Some bacteria use other pigments, and even sulfur compounds instead of water, for photosynthesis."]],
dna:[["Genetic technology","The Human Genome Project finished in 2003 after 13 years. CRISPR gene editing, developed in the 2010s, won Jennifer Doudna and Emmanuelle Charpentier the 2020 Nobel Prize in Chemistry."]],
bh:[["Sizes","Stellar black holes weigh a few to tens of solar masses, while supermassive ones at the centers of galaxies hold millions to billions. Sagittarius A* has about 4 million solar masses."]],
egypt:[["Daily life","Most Egyptians were farmers who relied on the Nile’s annual flood. They wrote on papyrus, made from a river reed, and used hieroglyphs alongside simpler scripts."]],
rome:[["Government","Rome became a republic in 509 BCE, ruled by the Senate and elected magistrates. Julius Caesar was assassinated in 44 BCE, and the republic gave way to emperors."]],
internet:[["How data travels","Information is split into packets that travel separately and are reassembled at their destination. Every device gets an IP address, and the Domain Name System turns names into those addresses."]],
elec:[["Generation","Most electricity comes from turbines spun by steam, water or wind, using Faraday’s principle of induction. Alternating current won out for long-distance transmission because transformers can easily raise and lower its voltage."],["Markets","In many countries electricity is traded in wholesale markets where prices follow supply and demand over short intervals. Britain, the Nordic countries and Australia were among the first to set up such markets in the 1990s."]],
evo:[["Mechanisms","Mutation supplies new variation, natural selection favors traits that aid survival and reproduction, and genetic drift shifts gene frequencies by chance. Antibiotic resistance is evolution visible within a human lifetime."]],
tect:[["Evidence","Alfred Wegener proposed continental drift in 1912. Matching fossils on separated continents, and the seafloor spreading discovered in the 1960s, convinced geologists."]],
comp:[["Personal computers","The 1970s and 1980s brought the Apple II, the IBM PC and graphical interfaces. The web and smartphones later put computing in billions of pockets."]],
ph:[["Regions and people","The country has three main island groups: Luzon, the Visayas and Mindanao. Well over 100 languages are spoken, and Spanish and American rule left deep marks on its culture."],["Economy","Money sent home by overseas Filipino workers is a major source of income, and the country is a leading center for business process outsourcing."]],
amazon:[["Threats","Large areas have been cleared for cattle ranching and soy farming, while Indigenous territories often show some of the lowest deforestation rates in the region."]],
ww2:[["Home fronts","Civilian economies were reorganized for war production and rationing was common. The Holocaust, the Nazi genocide of six million Jews, remains one of history’s greatest crimes."]],
space:[["Beyond the Moon","Robotic probes have visited every planet. Voyager 1, launched in 1977, entered interstellar space in 2012 and is the most distant human-made object."]],
climate:[["Responses","The 2015 Paris Agreement aims to hold warming well below 2°C above preindustrial levels. Solutions combine cutting emissions, protecting forests and adapting to changes already under way."]],
brain:[["Learning and memory","Memories form when connections between neurons strengthen, a process called plasticity. The hippocampus is key to forming new memories."]],
nuclear:[["Fusion","Fusion joins light nuclei, as in the Sun. In December 2022 the US National Ignition Facility produced more energy from a fusion target than the laser energy delivered to it, though not more than the facility consumed."]],
renew:[["Hydro and geothermal","Hydropower is the largest renewable source of electricity worldwide. Geothermal plants tap heat from underground and run around the clock, unlike solar and wind."]],
coldwar:[["Arms race and proxy wars","Both sides built nuclear arsenals that peaked at tens of thousands of warheads, and they fought through allies in places such as Korea, Vietnam and Afghanistan."]]};

;
