window.TERMS=["Algorithm|A step-by-step procedure for solving a problem.","Archipelago|A group or chain of islands.","Bandwidth|The maximum rate at which data can be transferred.","Binary|A number system that uses only 0 and 1.","Blackout|A complete loss of electric power over an area.","Calorie|A unit of energy; one food Calorie equals about 4,184 joules.","Catalyst|A substance that speeds up a reaction without being used up.","Chlorophyll|The green pigment that absorbs light for photosynthesis.","Climate change|A long-term shift in temperatures and weather patterns.","Colony|A territory ruled by another country.","Conductor|A material that lets electric current flow easily.","Continent|One of Earth’s large landmasses.","Crust|Earth’s thin outer solid layer.","Current|The flow of electric charge, measured in amperes.","Delta|A landform created where a river deposits sediment at its mouth.","Demand|The amount of a good, or of electricity, that buyers want at a given price or moment.","Dynasty|A line of rulers from the same family.","Electron|A negatively charged particle found in atoms.","Empire|A group of territories under one ruler or government.","Enzyme|A protein that speeds up reactions in living things.","Erosion|The wearing away of rock and soil by water, wind or ice.","Fossil|The preserved remains or traces of an ancient organism.","Fossil fuel|Coal, oil or gas formed from ancient living things.","Generator|A machine that converts mechanical energy into electricity.","Glacier|A large mass of ice that moves slowly over land.","Globalization|The growing connection of the world’s economies, cultures and people.","Grid|The network that carries electricity from generators to users.","Hertz|One cycle per second, the unit of frequency.","Hydroelectric|Describes electricity produced from flowing water.","Insulator|A material that resists the flow of electric current.","Isotope|One of several forms of an element with different numbers of neutrons.","Latitude|Distance north or south of the equator, measured in degrees.","Longitude|Distance east or west of the prime meridian, measured in degrees.","Magma|Molten rock beneath Earth’s surface.","Mantle|The thick layer of hot rock between Earth’s crust and core.","Mitosis|Cell division that produces two identical cells.","Molecule|Two or more atoms bonded together.","Neutron|An uncharged particle in the nucleus of an atom.","Orbit|The curved path of one object around another under gravity.","Peninsula|Land surrounded by water on three sides.","Plateau|A high, flat area of land.","Protein|A large molecule made of amino acids that does most of the work in cells.","Proton|A positively charged particle in the nucleus of an atom.","Renaissance|The European revival of art and learning from the 14th to the 17th centuries.","Resistance|The opposition a material offers to electric current, measured in ohms.","Revolution|A rapid, fundamental change in government or society.","Satellite|An object that orbits a larger body.","Sediment|Particles of rock and soil carried and deposited by water, wind or ice.","Spot price|The market price of a commodity for immediate delivery.","Strait|A narrow waterway connecting two larger bodies of water.","Substation|A facility that changes voltage levels within an electric power system.","Tectonic|Relating to the movement of Earth’s plates.","Transformer|A device that raises or lowers alternating-current voltage.","Tributary|A stream that flows into a larger river.","Virus|A tiny infectious agent that can reproduce only inside living cells.","Voltage|Electric potential difference, measured in volts."];

