window.TERMS=(window.TERMS||[]).concat(["Ancillary services|Support services, such as frequency control, that keep an electric grid stable.","Aquifer|An underground layer of rock that holds groundwater.","Atmosphere|The layer of gases surrounding a planet.","Bacteria|Single-celled organisms that have no nucleus.","Baseload|The minimum level of electricity demand that must be met continuously.","Biodiversity|The variety of life in an area.","Canopy|The upper layer of a forest.","Capacitor|A component that stores electric charge.","Capacity factor|The share of a power plant’s maximum possible output that it actually produces over time.","Carbon cycle|The movement of carbon among the air, oceans, land and living things.","Cartography|The making of maps.","Chromosome|A thread of DNA that carries genes.","Circuit|A closed path along which electric current can flow.","Civilization|A complex society with cities, government and writing.","Compound|A substance made of two or more elements bonded together.","Consumer|An organism that eats other organisms for energy.","Core|Earth’s hot central region.","Cyclone|A large rotating storm system.","Decomposer|An organism that breaks down dead matter.","Diaspora|A people living away from their ancestral homeland.","Dispatch|The scheduling of power plants to meet electricity demand.","Drought|A long period of unusually low rainfall.","Element|A substance made of only one kind of atom.","Equator|The imaginary line around Earth halfway between the poles.","Estuary|The wide mouth of a river where it meets the sea.","Fault|A fracture in Earth’s crust where blocks of rock move.","Feudalism|A medieval system in which land was held in exchange for service.","Fjord|A narrow sea inlet between steep cliffs, carved by a glacier.","Fusion|The joining of light atomic nuclei, which releases energy.","Genetics|The study of heredity and genes.","Geothermal|Relating to heat from inside Earth.","Hemisphere|One half of the globe.","Hormone|A chemical messenger made by glands.","Hurricane|A tropical cyclone in the Atlantic or eastern Pacific.","Hypothesis|A testable explanation for an observation.","Imperialism|The policy of extending a country’s power over other territories.","Inertia|The tendency of an object to resist changes in its motion.","Ion|An atom or molecule with an electric charge.","Isthmus|A narrow strip of land linking two larger land areas.","Lava|Magma that has reached Earth’s surface.","Load|The amount of power drawn from an electric grid.","Magnetosphere|The region around a planet shaped by its magnetic field.","Mass|The amount of matter in an object.","Megawatt|One million watts of power.","Meteor|A streak of light made by a space rock burning up in the atmosphere.","Migration|The movement of people or animals from one place to another.","Mineral|A naturally occurring solid with a definite chemical makeup.","Monarchy|Government headed by a king or queen.","Nebula|A cloud of gas and dust in space.","Neuron|A nerve cell.","Nutrient|A substance that organisms need to live and grow.","Ohm|The unit of electrical resistance.","Oxidation|A chemical reaction in which a substance loses electrons.","Parliament|A legislative body of elected representatives.","Plankton|Tiny organisms that drift in oceans and lakes.","Pollination|The transfer of pollen that allows plants to reproduce.","Population|All the individuals of a species living in an area.","Prime meridian|The line of 0° longitude, which runs through Greenwich.","Radiation|Energy that travels as waves or particles.","Reactor|A device in which a nuclear chain reaction is sustained.","Refraction|The bending of light as it passes between materials.","Savanna|A tropical grassland with scattered trees.","Solstice|The day with the most or least daylight in the year.","Spectrum|The range of wavelengths of light or other radiation.","Supernova|The explosion of a massive star at the end of its life.","Taiga|A northern forest of conifers.","Tide|The rise and fall of the sea caused by the Moon and Sun.","Trade winds|Steady winds that blow toward the equator.","Tsunami|A giant sea wave caused by an undersea earthquake or eruption.","Tundra|A cold, treeless region with frozen subsoil.","Turbine|A machine whose blades spin when fluid flows past them.","Typhoon|A tropical cyclone in the northwest Pacific.","Vaccine|A preparation that trains the immune system against a disease.","Watershed|The area of land that drains into a river.","Wavelength|The distance between successive wave crests.","Weathering|The breakdown of rock by air, water and living things."]);

;
