window.EXTRA=Object.assign(window.EXTRA||{},{
stars:[["Measuring distance","A light-year is the distance light travels in a year, about 9.46 trillion km. The nearest star beyond the Sun, Proxima Centauri, is about 4.2 light-years away."]],
greece:[["Science and the arts","Euclid and Archimedes laid foundations for geometry and physics, and Hippocrates is called the father of medicine. Tragedy and comedy as theater began in Athens."]],
mongol:[["Governance","A strict legal code, the Yassa, and a highly mobile cavalry held the empire together. After Genghis Khan died in 1227 it split into several khanates ruled by his descendants."]],
frrev:[["Estates and ideas","French society was divided into three estates: the clergy, the nobility and everyone else, who carried most of the taxes. Enlightenment thinkers such as Rousseau and Voltaire shaped the revolution’s ideals of liberty and equality."]],
wwi:[["Alliances","Europe was split between the Entente of France, Russia and Britain and the Central Powers led by Germany and Austria-Hungary. Italy joined the Entente in 1915, and the United States entered the war in 1917."]],
phrev:[["Key figures","Besides Rizal and Bonifacio, leaders included Emilio Aguinaldo, Apolinario Mabini and Gregoria de Jesús. Rizal’s writings inspired reform, though he did not support the armed uprising."]],
reef:[["Coral and algae","Corals live in partnership with tiny algae that give them color and food. When stressed by heat they expel the algae and turn white, a process called bleaching."]],
arctic:[["Ice and shipping","Summer sea ice has shrunk markedly since satellite records began in 1979. Less ice may open Arctic shipping routes such as the Northern Sea Route and the Northwest Passage."]],
volc:[["Types","Shield volcanoes such as Mauna Loa have gentle slopes built from runny lava, while stratovolcanoes such as Mount Fuji and Mayon are steep and can erupt explosively. Supervolcanoes such as Yellowstone erupt very rarely."]],
himal:[["People and culture","Sherpas, Tibetans and many other peoples live in the high valleys, where Buddhism and Hinduism shape local life."]],
med:[["Trade and empires","Phoenician traders spread the alphabet around its shores, and the Romans called it Mare Nostrum, meaning our sea."]],
quake:[["Preparedness","Buildings with flexible frames and base isolation survive shaking better, and the standard advice during a quake is to drop, cover and hold on. Early warning systems can give seconds of notice."]],
ai:[["Language models","Large language models learn patterns from huge amounts of text in order to predict and generate language. They can write and summarize but can also state falsehoods confidently, so their output needs checking."]],
battery:[["Types","Lead-acid batteries still start most cars, alkaline cells power remote controls, and lithium-ion cells run phones and electric vehicles. Each type trades off cost, weight and lifespan."]],
rail:[["Networks","Electrified lines and metro systems move millions of people each day in cities such as Tokyo. Freight trains carry bulk goods such as coal, grain and containers across continents."]],
phone:[["Switchboards to digital","Early calls were connected by human operators at switchboards. Automatic exchanges, fiber-optic cables and digital switching made modern global calling possible."]],
sat:[["Space debris","Dead satellites and rocket fragments orbit as space debris, and even tiny pieces can damage spacecraft at orbital speeds. Tracking networks follow tens of thousands of objects."]],
wcycle:[["Groundwater and rivers","Some rain soaks into the ground and becomes groundwater, which aquifers store and which supplies wells and springs. Rivers carry runoff back to the sea, completing the cycle."]],
newton:[["Applications and limits","Rocket launches, car crash design and the motion of planets all follow from Newton’s laws. They break down only at extreme speeds, where relativity is needed, and at atomic scales, where quantum mechanics takes over."]],
mendel:[["Modern genetics","Genes sit on chromosomes, and many traits depend on several genes at once, so inheritance is often more complex than in Mendel’s peas. The environment can also affect how genes are switched on."]]});

