window.TERMS=(window.TERMS||[]).concat(["Acceleration|The rate at which velocity changes.","Alloy|A metal made by combining two or more elements.","Amplitude|The maximum extent of a wave’s oscillation.","Anthropology|The study of human societies and cultures.","Apogee|The point in an orbit farthest from Earth.","Asteroid|A rocky body orbiting the Sun that is smaller than a planet.","Astronomy|The scientific study of objects beyond Earth.","Aurora|Glowing light in polar skies caused by charged particles striking the atmosphere.","Axis|The imaginary line about which a body rotates.","Botany|The study of plants.","Cambrian|The geologic period beginning about 539 million years ago, when many animal groups appeared.","Carnivore|An animal that eats mainly meat.","Census|An official count of a population.","Cirrus|High, thin, wispy clouds.","Colonialism|Control of one people or territory by another.","Comet|An icy body that grows a glowing tail near the Sun.","Congestion|A grid condition in which transmission limits stop the cheapest power from flowing.","Constitution|The fundamental rules by which a state is governed.","Cumulus|Fluffy, heaped clouds.","Cuneiform|An ancient wedge-shaped writing system.","Curtailment|Deliberately reducing a power plant’s output, for example when the grid cannot take more.","Diameter|A straight line through the center of a circle.","Diffusion|The spread of particles from high to low concentration.","Dune|A hill of sand formed by wind.","Ecology|The study of how organisms interact with their environment.","Embargo|A ban on trade with a country.","Endangered|At risk of extinction.","Entropy|A measure of disorder in a system.","Equinox|A day when day and night are nearly equal in length.","Extinction|The complete disappearance of a species.","Fermentation|The chemical breakdown of sugars by yeast or bacteria.","Fiber optic|A thin glass strand that carries data as pulses of light.","Fission|The splitting of a heavy atomic nucleus, which releases energy.","Friction|A force that resists motion between surfaces.","Fungus|An organism such as a mushroom or mold that digests food outside its body.","Galaxy|A vast system of stars, gas and dust held together by gravity.","Geology|The study of Earth’s rocks and structure.","Habitat|The natural home of an organism.","Herbivore|An animal that eats mainly plants.","Humidity|The amount of water vapor in the air.","Igneous|Describes rock formed from cooled magma or lava.","Infrastructure|The basic systems, such as roads and power grids, that a society relies on.","Interconnector|A transmission link between two power systems or regions.","Intermittent|Describes a power source, such as wind or solar, whose output varies with the weather.","Lens|A curved piece of transparent material that bends light.","Lunar|Relating to the Moon.","Mammal|A warm-blooded animal that nurses its young.","Merit order|A ranking of power plants by cost, used to decide which run first.","Metamorphic|Describes rock changed by heat and pressure.","Meteorite|A space rock that reaches Earth’s surface.","Microbe|A microscopic organism.","Nomad|A member of a people who move from place to place.","Omnivore|An animal that eats both plants and animals.","Ozone|A gas whose layer in the stratosphere absorbs ultraviolet light.","Peak demand|The highest level of electricity use in a given period.","Perihelion|The point in an orbit nearest the Sun.","Pharaoh|A ruler of ancient Egypt.","Pressure|Force applied per unit area.","Prism|A transparent shape that splits light into colors.","Quasar|An extremely bright galactic core powered by a supermassive black hole.","Reservoir|An artificial lake used to store water.","Reserve margin|Extra generating capacity above expected peak demand.","Sedimentary|Describes rock formed from compressed sediment.","Seismograph|An instrument that records earthquake waves.","Stratosphere|The atmospheric layer above the troposphere.","Tariff|A tax on imported goods.","Troposphere|The lowest layer of the atmosphere, where weather occurs.","Velocity|Speed in a given direction.","Zoology|The study of animals."]);

