frog:"Many frogs absorb water and breathe partly through their skin.",
tiger:"No two tigers have exactly the same stripe pattern.",
bat:"Bats are the only mammals capable of true flight.",
jupiter:"Ganymede, a moon of Jupiter, is larger than the planet Mercury.",
saturn:"Saturn’s rings are often only about 10 meters thick.",
milky:"The Sun takes roughly 225 to 250 million years to orbit the center of the Milky Way.",
iss:"The International Space Station circles Earth about 16 times a day.",
eclipse:"A total solar eclipse is visible from any particular place only about once every few hundred years.",
pulsar:"A teaspoon of neutron star material would weigh about a billion tonnes.",
supdem:"In electricity markets, prices can shift within minutes because supply and demand must match in real time.",
money:"The first coins were made in Lydia, in present-day Turkey, around 600 BCE.",
trade:"Container shipping began in 1956 and sharply cut the cost of moving goods.",
rice:"The International Rice Research Institute was founded in Los Baños, Philippines, in 1960.",
